From: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] crypto: bcm - reject a CCM IV with an invalid length field

The first byte of a CCM IV holds L' = L - 1, which must be 1 to 7.
The generic implementation rejects other values with -EINVAL. The
driver masks the byte to its low three bits and encrypts with the
resulting length field instead:

  alg: aead: ccm-aes-iproc encryption unexpectedly succeeded on test
  vector "random: alen=0 plen=445 authsize=16 klen=32 novrfy=0";
  expected_error=-22, ...

Reject these IVs. rfc4309 builds its own IV with a fixed L and is not
affected.

Fixes: 9d12ba86f818 ("crypto: brcm - Add Broadcom SPU driver")
Signed-off-by: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/crypto/bcm/cipher.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/crypto/bcm/cipher.c
+++ b/drivers/crypto/bcm/cipher.c
@@ -2716,6 +2716,10 @@ static int aead_enqueue(struct aead_request *req, bool is_encrypt)
 	if (ctx->is_esp && crypto_ipsec_check_assoclen(req->assoclen))
 		return -EINVAL;
 
+	if (ctx->cipher.mode == CIPHER_MODE_CCM && !ctx->is_esp &&
+	    (req->iv[0] < 1 || req->iv[0] > 7))
+		return -EINVAL;
+
 	rctx->gfp = (req->base.flags & CRYPTO_TFM_REQ_MAY_SLEEP) ?
 		       GFP_KERNEL : GFP_ATOMIC;
 	rctx->parent = &req->base;
